"""Mutations of part 8c-ii's GEffects code (src/game/geffects.*: shadows, face textures, uniforms,
shattered glass; the S_ShadowParams defaults) for ../mutfast.py with the world build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_8c2.py --models DIR --build build_world.bat --check check_world.py

DIR holds a .txt per mission ("mission NAME"; the tests run the same in each). Each mutation should
make check_world.py fail (or the harness crash / hang). Generated from the 8c-ii lines only (a
comparison, a number, an operator or a statement per line), then pruned. Left out as equivalent
(14): the shadow search's 2 as another value (the first shadow found stays found); the face search's
list clearing (a match returns at once); MoveForeignFrames' SetPosInline / SetRot (LinkTo without
I3DLINK_KEEP_WORLD keeps the local place); the shard normal's unit test against 1 (normalizing a unit
square changes nothing) or 1.5, and its 1e-8 threshold (squares of floats do not land on them); the
degenerate normal's signs (< or <= 0 of a component known not to be 0); the faces loop's <= 6 (a
write past the vector, undefined); the 1-2 edge's tie with 0-1 (decided before); the 1-2 case's
b = &p2 (already so; the line was removed); the edge's square test (1 after normalizing);
uniform != -2 (GetItemDef(-1) is null). 1 more did not compile and was dropped.

Run 1 (255): 224 caught, 30 survived, 1 not built. New cases for 16: a shadow under another model's
shadow; targets first among the children and nested; the copy's rotation (not the new model's); the
human as member 0; the first load's flags; the stages 0..7 only; a tilted face's normal (the y term),
a tiny one along z, one just under the threshold (kept unnormalized); a face off the origin; a split
off the origin with distinct texture coordinates; the 0-1 case's texture coordinates. Run 2 (240):
238 caught; the stage check widened (-1 too). Run 3 (240): all caught.
"""
